From 1edbfdb93f0f786ba383ba91b23a31b19e328f78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:13:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] engine: spec lanes review fixes (opt-in
 STRATA_SPEC_LANES=2)

- giveback copies only the cells the lane drafter holds for the slot's
  conversation (below lane_dk; nothing when it is unknown)
- a lane runs its own request's PCIe shares (stored per lane slot at
  admission), not the last request's
- catch-up: the row is copied on the batch window's stream into one of
  two buffers per lane; the batch stream waits on the drafter only before
  reusing a buffer (not on the previous prefill every time)
- the lanes' window and commit graphs are captured at boot, so the boot
  lines and the LOW check count them
- lanes_asked includes the refusals known before the caches; the lane
  reserve is left out of --layer-split auto's search
- test knobs: STRATA_SPEC_LANES_NOSTART=1 (everything but lane starts:
  batch-path byte identity, overhead A/B) and STRATA_SPEC_LANES_HOLD=1
  (a lone fresh lane slot waits for the next line: exactness drive)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
